title A cell that counted a room -- the stashed lap lands, and the half it left open was already false
prompt fleet baton, Petrichor seat -- open the round, take the lane's next lap
rota lap 4626, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; TAME Core, single-stranded, GAUGE_STYLE, read through the threshold page: a boundary is tested by pressing on it, and if the hand passes through, the boundary was a wish
think Round-open named 1 session log standing in the dead-letter box and nowhere else. The cold roster pass reddened `stash_record` on the same fact. Reds first, so I read it before taking new work.
think The unlanded record was my own: `session-logs/date/20260911/20260911-053329_the-count-inside-a-name.kyri`, in stash@{0} with its whole lap -- the crushed_index title reading, its control legs, the blog door, the card. That lap answered Keaton's own open ask and died before its commit, so landing it IS the lap rather than a chore beside it.
think A stale roster lock held the run at first -- pid 2949843, launch_head `6d8838acaf`, verdict already fixed at tree_moved. `fleet_call.sh --pattern standing_equipment_run --signal TERM` released it through the runner's own EXIT trap; the lock directory was reaped rather than left.
think Pressing on the restored guard's own stated limit while the pass ran: it walls a count in a declared index's TITLE and leaves a count in a CELL open on purpose. So I walked the four declared indexes for typed counts and compared each against the room on disk.
obs The hand went through. `docs-geode/wiki/README.md` read *the four announcements in `press/`* while SEVEN pieces stand. True the day it was written, `20260906`; false from `20260908`, when the Radiator essay landed as the room's fifth piece. Three days wrong, in a table whose own guard walks every page under the shelf.
obs The card graded the page A/96 with `truth=100` before the repair, and it was right to: `truth_mode=counted` reads whether a cited path resolves, and a stale number is no path at all. The same blind reading is recorded twice in `.claude/rules/quality-assurance.md`; this is a third, found by hand rather than by the card.
obs The repair takes the shelf's own seated move, now made four times: a cell points at the room and the room counts itself. No new guard, because the class on my shelf has a precedent rather than a gap.
obs No red booked. The unlanded record was a lap that died, repaired by landing it, and the false cell is a claim that went stale rather than an instrument that lied.
